   "subject": "Re: Showing POSIXt object with Shiny renderTable",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "renderTable uses xtable() to generate the output, and it looks like xtable doesn&#39;t play well with dates in general:<div><br></div><div><div>library(xtable)</div><div>dat &lt;- data.frame(date=as.POSIXlt(Sys.time()), x=1:5)</div>\r\n\r\n<div>print(xtable(dat))</div><div># Error in Math.POSIXt(x + ifelse(x == 0, 1, 0)) : </div><div>#   &#39;abs&#39; not defined for &quot;POSIXt&quot; objects</div><div><br></div></div><div>I&#39;ve filed an issue here:</div>\r\n\r\n<div>  <a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/129\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/129&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409538635000&amp;usg=AOvVaw37VHB6biim6PGKjzDsBQLV\">https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/129</a></div><div><br></div><div>In the meantime, a workaround is to convert the relevant columns to characters:</div><div>\r\n\r\n  <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8652674/r-xtable-and-dates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8652674/r-xtable-and-dates&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409538635000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QeuJmLgJUsgIYUklOhh7S\">http://stackoverflow.com/questions/8652674/r-xtable-and-dates</a></div><div><br></div><div>-Winston</div><div><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Mar 20, 2013 at 2:32 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">timo...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br>\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
